down with communism that's the message  from citizens in cuba as many have taken  to the streets to protest the government  thanks for joining us at 11 i'm denise  faldis and i'm brian loftis these are  the large protests on the island in  decades as cubans complain about the  lack of food the lack of medicine  the country facing a crisis aggravated  by the covid pandemic  protests have spilled onto the streets  really all over the world including las  vegas boulevard  orco mana is on the strip tonight with  their message denise and brian hundreds  of people took to the las vegas trip  tonight  to stand in solidarity with the  protesters in cuba  for them this is all about showing their  support and also calling on the u.s  government to take action  around three to four hundred protesters  marched along the las vegas strip  tuesday night they started at the  boulevard in sahara and made their way  south many were holding cuban flags and  also signs  saying sos cuba some protesters drove  down the strip in their cars  too this is all in solidarity with the  recent unrest in cuba  resulting in the largest protests we've  seen in that country in decades  protesters there are fighting against  the communist regime which they say has  oppressed them for decades  but their calls for justice this time  around have been triggered  by food shortages rising prices and the  cuban government's response to rising  covenanting infections  now communities across the u.s including  here in las vegas have taken to the  streets  protesters we spoke to say they felt  compelled to speak out  i think it's very important for our  voice to be heard  since we are such a big country the more  we go out  the better it is if cuba is on the  streets  we can be on the streets as well we need  everybody to open their eyes  because the reality is that  we're hurting a lot protesters are also  calling on the u.s government to  intervene to help the people of cuba  president biden released a statement  monday saying in part  quote the united states calls on the  cuban regime to hear their people  and serve their needs at this vital  moment end quote but it's unclear if any  policy changes relating to cuba  will be on the horizon  metro police police officers were  following along with the protesters  as they marched south on this strip to  make sure people stayed safe  and it appears everything remained  peaceful tonight reporting live on the  las vegas strip orca mana 8 news now
 

